---
import numbers from "../data/numbers.json";
import { fmtScore, frac } from "../lib/format";
const m = numbers.internal;
---

<section id="top" class="relative overflow-hidden" aria-labelledby="hero-heading">
  <div
    class="pointer-events-none absolute inset-x-0 top-0 h-px bg-gradient-to-r from-transparent via-gold to-transparent"
    aria-hidden="true"
  ></div>
  <div class="wrap pt-16 pb-14 sm:pt-24 sm:pb-20">
    <p class="kicker mb-8">
      <span>Open source</span>
      <span class="num" aria-hidden="true">/</span>
      <span>Apache-2.0</span>
      <span class="num" aria-hidden="true">/</span>
      <span>Pre-release 0.1.0.dev0</span>
      <span class="num" aria-hidden="true">/</span>
      <span>Python tasks</span>
    </p>

    <h1
      id="hero-heading"
      class="font-serif italic font-semibold text-display leading-[0.95] tracking-[-0.03em] max-w-5xl"
    >
      Audit the tests that score your agents.
    </h1>

    <p class="mt-8 max-w-2xl text-lg sm:text-xl text-paper/90 leading-relaxed">
      Aethens is an open-source Python CLI and GitHub Action that audits the
      verifiers of RL environments and code-task benchmarks by running them in a
      Docker sandbox. Every finding comes with evidence and a one-line repro
      command. The checks themselves have published precision and recall you can
      reproduce.
    </p>

    <p class="mt-5 max-w-2xl text-sm text-muted">
      Not on PyPI yet. Install from a clone of{' '}
      <a class="prose-link" href="https://github.com/beastrog/aethens">the repository</a>.
      Needs Docker and Python 3.11+. No LLMs, no network access for task code, no telemetry.
    </p>

    <div class="mt-12 grid gap-4 lg:grid-cols-2">
      <div>
        <p class="cmd-label">Install and run</p>
        <pre class="cmd" tabindex="0"><code>git clone https://github.com/beastrog/aethens.git
cd aethens
python -m pip install .
docker pull python:3.12-slim
aethens audit path/to/task --format markdown</code></pre>
      </div>
      <div>
        <p class="cmd-label">GitHub Action</p>
        <pre class="cmd" tabindex="0"><code>- uses: beastrog/aethens@main
  with:
    path: path/to/tasks
    budget: standard
    fail-on: error
    seed: "0"</code></pre>
        <p class="mt-2 text-xs text-muted">
          Pin a release tag once one exists. <code class="text-gold">@main</code> is pre-release.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <dl
      class="mt-12 grid grid-cols-2 gap-px bg-line sm:grid-cols-4 border border-line"
      aria-label={`Internal bench summary, ${m.label}`}
    >
      <div class="bg-ink px-4 py-4 sm:px-5">
        <dt class="metric-label">Precision</dt>
        <dd class="font-serif italic text-4xl sm:text-5xl leading-none">{fmtScore(m.precision)}</dd>
      </div>
      <div class="bg-ink px-4 py-4 sm:px-5">
        <dt class="metric-label">Recall</dt>
        <dd class="font-serif italic text-4xl sm:text-5xl leading-none">
          {fmtScore(m.recall)}
          <span class="block font-mono text-[0.7rem] not-italic tracking-normal text-muted mt-2 normal-case">
            {frac(m.found, m.planted)} planted defects
          </span>
        </dd>
      </div>
      <div class="bg-ink px-4 py-4 sm:px-5">
        <dt class="metric-label">False positives</dt>
        <dd class="font-serif italic text-4xl sm:text-5xl leading-none">{m.false_positives}</dd>
      </div>
      <div class="bg-ink px-4 py-4 sm:px-5">
        <dt class="metric-label">Reward-hacking</dt>
        <dd class="font-serif italic text-4xl sm:text-5xl leading-none">{frac(m.reward_hack.found, m.reward_hack.labelled)}</dd>
      </div>
    </dl>
    <p class="mt-3 font-mono text-[0.7rem] text-muted tracking-wide">
      Internal self-authored bench, 34 tasks, seed 0, budget standard.{' '}
      {m.label}.
      External-bench figures, including a weak C004 precision of {fmtScore(numbers.external.c004.precision)}, are in{' '}
      <a class="prose-link" href="#accuracy">Published accuracy</a>.
    </p>
  </div>
</section>
